"use client";
/**
 * Documents — the clinical document editor (source L14341–L20842): library and template gallery, the block editor (ribbon,
 * pages / plan pane, canvas, properties, components), pagination and columns, tables with formulas, charts and themes,
 * comments / history / assistant drawers, find and replace, quality checker, multi-person signing, export to every
 * format with the print centre, import v2 and its review, exact PDF forms, Word-exact documents, "open as is" (flow,
 * spreadsheet and slide engines, IndexedDB store) with save back to Word, entities, generic building blocks, and the
 * bundled remotion-documents engine (RD) and PDF / ZIP writer (RDX), with their 97 overrides.
 *
 * Deliberate structure (ADR-04 exception, as for the other native apps): the source builds the app from string
 * templates written with innerHTML and patched in place. It is ported as a typed imperative island; `dcBody()` builds and
 * wires the `.dc` element exactly as in the source and DocumentsApp.tsx places it in the window body. The code below is
 * the source's own text (templates byte-identical) with types added; only the OS integration (L15405–L15420), the
 * first-open wrapper of dcOpen (L20275) and the cross-tab listener (L21041) are replaced by the React window wiring
 * (src/apps/documents/DocumentsApp.tsx) and the shell (APP_WINDOWS.documents, dock entry, osRelabel).
 *
 * Overrides: the 97 functions the source redefines later are declared `let dcX=function…` at the same place (nothing
 * calls them while the module loads). Overrides that forward `arguments` (`_x.apply(this,arguments)`) take an explicit
 * rest parameter and forward `[params…, ...more]` — the same values (no callee reads `arguments.length`).
 *
 * Other documented edits: the source's module-level document / window listeners (69 + 4) are registered on first mount
 * (dcInstallGlobal); `e.target` reads go through `tgt(e)`; `lang` is the OS language getter `lang()`; the front-window
 * test `shell.lastElementChild===win` is the window stack's `isTop("os:documents")`; mixed `let` declarations whose
 * other names are never re-assigned are split into `let` / `const` in the same order (lint prefer-const).
 *
 * Approved fix D-D04 (doc 09 §4): Ctrl+P prints the document only when Documents is the front window (the source also
 * captured it while another window was focused, L19576).
 *
 * Types: the document model (DcDoc / DcPage / DcBlock) was sampled from the source's own seed and templates; the
 * engine-specific shapes (Word runs and paragraphs, export flow, import items, signatures, exact forms, …) are declared
 * below. Values the source stores in loosely-shaped bags are asserted to their type where they are read.
 *
 * The download (dcSaveFile) and ZIP code here are the source's own copies; src/lib/download.ts and src/lib/zip.ts hold
 * the same algorithms for the other apps (B-17).
 */
